    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361-a6">

                <pb facs="0472" n="376" xml:id="pg376"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lafontant to Mr.
                            Powell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State for Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Port au Prince, Haiti</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1899-03-31"><hi rendition="#italic">March 31,
                                1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I hasten to acknowledge reception
                    of your important communication of yesterday’s date, which I immediately
                    transmitted to the department of interior to obtain the necessary
                    information.</p>
                <p>However, and before even those informations, I can give you the assurance that it
                    can never have entered in the intention of my colleague, Mr. the Secretary of
                    State of the Interior, to give orders that may be of the nature to bring a
                    violation of international laws and the violation of the dwelling of an
                    accredited agent of the United States.</p>
                <p>If a like circumstance has been able to take place, I remain convinced that it
                    can only have been in consequence of badly interpreted instructions.</p>
                <p>I take note that the Cubans residing in the Republic are under the protection of
                    the Government of the United States of America, and I beg you to accept, Mr.
                    Minister, the renewed assurance of my high consideration, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">N. S. Lafontant.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
